// Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` (same folder) and fill in the values.
// `Secrets.xcconfig` is gitignored; this template is committed.
//
// Both values come from the Supabase dashboard, Project Settings → API.
//
// SUPABASE_HOST is the project URL with `https://` REMOVED. In an xcconfig,
// `//` begins a comment, so pasting the full URL would silently truncate it to
// `https:`. The scheme is added back in Swift.
//
//   Project URL   https://abcdefghijklm.supabase.co
//   SUPABASE_HOST abcdefghijklm.supabase.co
//
// SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the publishable ("anon") key, not the service role key.
// The service role key must never be shipped in an app — it bypasses every
// row-level security policy. The anon key is designed to be public.

SUPABASE_HOST = your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-publishable-anon-key
